-- id: exp6928-sota-runtime-receipt-qualification
-  title: Dual-GPU SOTA runtime receipt qualification
-  track: infrastructure
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: claude
-  model: opus
-  requires_gpu: true
-  max_turns: 100
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 360
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.607
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6928_sota_runtime_receipt_qualification.json
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6924 made the task-owned runtime receipt helper adoption-ready with deterministic CPU
-    fixtures. Its honest verdict remained null because it did not prove the contract on a real
-    SOTA dual-GPU subprocess. V607 needs one advisory hardware receipt before later compute claims.
-    No science task gates on this infrastructure task.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/task_runtime_receipts.py
-    - {project_root}/scripts/experiment_template.py
-    - {project_root}/scripts/inference_sota_models.py
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6924_task_runtime_receipt_adoption.json
-    - {project_root}/tests/python/test_inference_sota_models.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md
-
-    TASK:
-    Qualify the existing receipt helper on a bounded live run of all three mandated local GGUF
-    model families. Prove task ownership, runner identity, CUDA devices, offload, phase intervals,
-    cache state, sequential model lifecycle, and teardown. Do not build a second telemetry system.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require two authenticated RTX 3090 CUDA devices, cached or resolvable GGUF
-       files, the existing receipt helper, and enough disk. On failure, write
-       blocked_sota_runtime_receipt_qualification with gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-REPORT-6928 and tests first. Cover PID and GPU ownership, monotonic phases, missing
-       teardown, UUID mismatch, cache hit and miss, sequential load, and fresh-process replay.
-    2. Define MODEL_SPECS with unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF,
-       unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF, and unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF. Use cached_sota_pair or
-       the current resolver. Do not call AutoTokenizer on a GGUF repository ID.
-    3. Run one short deterministic prompt per model. Load models sequentially. Record exact
-       quantization, model file, runner, command, child PID, GPU UUIDs, layer offload, context,
-       cache state, sampled VRAM, utilization, and teardown.
-    4. Re-read the receipt in a fresh process. Recompute phase ordering, device ownership,
-       concurrency, teardown, and total duration from rows.
-    5. Reject a copied receipt, a cross-process receipt, an unresolved GPU identity, or missing
-       teardown. Keep failed model rows.
-    6. Set sota_runtime_receipt_ready_score=1 only when all three model families have valid
-       task-owned CUDA receipts and fresh-process replay passes.
-    7. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, the applicable model-loading smoke check,
-       artifact-convention audit, verdict-row consistency lint, docs audit, and root-clutter checks.
-    8. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific principle per required field
-       and sota_runtime_receipt_ready_score; preconditions_checked; inference_substrate
-       (task_owned_local_gguf_cuda_inference); duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; rows;
-       model_specs; model_rows; model_file_rows; runner_selection_rows; process_lineage_rows;
-       task_phase_timing_rows; task_gpu_telemetry_rows; model_concurrency_rows;
-       server_lifecycle_rows; cache_state_rows; teardown_rows; fresh_process_recheck_rows;
-       forged_receipt_rejection_rows; task_runtime_receipt; random_seed;
-       reproducibility_checksum; sota_runtime_receipt_ready_score; gate_check_summary with the
-       failed check, expected value, and observed value for any blocked verdict;
-       verifier_is_oracle (false); verdict_class (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked |
-       disqualified | partial); honest_verdict (terminal and prefixed complete_ or blocked_).
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6928_sota_runtime_receipt_qualification.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
