-- id: exp6929-three-family-span-acquisition
-  title: Three-family live span-first relation acquisition
-  track: acquisition
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: claude
-  model: sonnet
-  requires_gpu: true
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 720
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.607
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6929_three_family_span_acquisition.json
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6926 produced an exact 69-row span-first fixture across 15 family-label cells. It proved
-    offsets, aliases, direction, and labels, but it used a deterministic fixture and earned a
-    circular-positive verdict. Exp6915's free-form relation bank qualified only eight events.
-    V607 must test live held-out acquisition with every required SOTA family.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md, {project_root}/CODEX.md, and
-      {project_root}/research-program.md
-    - {project_root}/scripts/experiments/experiment_6926_span_first_relation_fixture.py
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6926_span_first_relation_fixture.json
-    - {project_root}/scripts/experiments/experiment_6912_alias_safe_relation_corpus_reducer.py
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6915_qualified_relation_event_bank.json
-    - {project_root}/scripts/experiment_template.py and
-      {project_root}/scripts/inference_sota_models.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md
-
-    TASK:
-    Run live span-first relation acquisition on held-out prompts with all three required GGUF
-    families. Require two verbatim source spans before a directed typed relation. Keep hidden
-    labels out of prompts and reprompts. Preserve all malformed, timed-out, and failed rows.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require the Exp6926 fixture contract and source hashes, held-out source text,
-       cached or resolvable mandated models, dual CUDA, and exact offset utilities. On failure,
-       write blocked_three_family_span_acquisition with gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-REPORT-6929 and tests before implementation. Cover Unicode byte offsets, duplicate
-       spans, reversed direction, aliases, missing spans, invalid JSON, and hidden-label isolation.
-    2. Define MODEL_SPECS with unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF,
-       unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF, and unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF. Use the current cached SOTA
-       resolver. Legacy small models may run smoke tests only.
-    3. Freeze held-out prompt IDs, source hashes, five relation families, seeds, decoding settings,
-       and at least six examples per model-family cell before inference.
-    4. Ask each model to copy span A and span B verbatim, then return one directed relation type.
-       Do not expose offsets, aliases, relation labels, exact-checker output, or prior failures.
-    5. Map copied bytes to offsets with exact code. Reject ambiguous matches rather than choosing
-       an offset. Normalize aliases only after both spans are grounded.
-    6. Save one row per attempted model-prompt-seed tuple with raw output, parse state, spans,
-       offsets, directed relation, token budget, runner receipt, and failure reason.
-    7. Set span_acquisition_bank_ready_score=1 only when all 15 model-family cells meet the frozen
-       attempt count and every attempt has a terminal row. This is readiness, not accuracy.
-    8. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, the applicable live model check,
-       artifact-convention audit, verdict-row consistency lint, docs audit, and root-clutter checks.
-    9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific principle per required field
-       and span_acquisition_bank_ready_score; preconditions_checked; inference_substrate
-       (live_local_gguf_span_first_relation_acquisition); duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; rows;
-       per_game_results; model_specs; model_rows; model_family_cell_rows; heldout_split_hashes;
-       source_text_rows; raw_output_rows; span_grounding_rows; offset_rows; alias_rows;
-       direction_rows; parse_failure_rows; timeout_rows; hidden_label_isolation_rows;
-       task_runtime_receipt; random_seed; reproducibility_checksum;
-       span_acquisition_bank_ready_score; gate_check_summary with the failed check, expected value,
-       and observed value for any blocked verdict; verifier_is_oracle (false);
-       verdict_class (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial);
-       honest_verdict (terminal and prefixed complete_ or blocked_).
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6929_three_family_span_acquisition.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
